%%HP: T(0)A(D)F(.);
@ SCNR
@ Arguments: A numerical matrix of the form
@  
@[ [ CHANNEL   FREQUENCY DELAY LOCKOUT PRIORITY] 
@  [ CHANNEL   FREQUENCY DELAY LOCKOUT PRIORITY]
@  [ CHANNEL   FREQUENCY DELAY LOCKOUT PRIORITY] ]
@
@ 
@ where:   CHANNEL is any number from 1 to 20.
@	 Most Radio Shack scanners have 10 banks of 20 channels for a total of 200.
@  Suggestion: Keep ten different matrices, one per 20-channel bank.
@	 Since my scanner (Pro-2018/20-424) only suports this format, this is the only one
@	 available in this software.
@	 (http://support.radioshack.com/support_tutorials/communications/20-424.htm)
@
@	 FREQUENCY is any number of the form xxx.xxxx which corresponds to a frequency
@	 available to the scanner. If you send invalid frequencies, the scanner will stop
@	 the transfer and show an error message on its screen.  You may have to
@  turn the scanner off and on to go back to normal operation.
@
@	 DELAY is either 0 or 1.
@		0 means no 2 sec. delay before resumming scanning.
@		1 means 2 sec. delay before resumming scanning.
@
@	 LOCKOUT is either 0 or 1.
@		0 means use this frequency
@		1 means do not use this frequency
@
@	 PRIORITY is either 0 or 1.
@		0 means this is not priority frequency (see yous scanner's manual for details)
@		1 means this is a priority frequency
@
@  Important: Make sure your calcualtor display is set to STD in the modes menu.
@             Engineering or Fixed displays may not work right.
@
@  Note: The type of scanners this sofware talks to, do not talk back. All
@        communication is 1-way.  The only acknowledgement shows up
@        in the scanners screen.
@
@ Author: Pepin Torres, P.E. - Waltham, Massachusetts, USA
@ E-mail: pepin [dot] torres {at} g m a i l (dot) com
@ Version: 1.0
@ Date: 02/20/2009
@ Created using HPUserEdit 5 [http://www.gaak.org/hpuser]

´ ç SCNRDATA 
  
   ´  
      @ Determine size of array and save it
      @-------------------------------------
      SCNRDATA SIZE LISTç DROP DROP DUP
      IF 20 > THEN "Sending first 20 entries only!" MSGBOX 20 'ENTRIES' STO
      ELSE 'ENTRIES' STO END
            
      @ Make START string: Header, Size, Command, Argument, Checksum 
      @-------------------------------------
      129 CHR 4 CHR  + 1 CHR +  1 CHR  + ENTRIES CHR + 
      'STARTSTR' STO
      
      @ Calculate checksum (sum of all chars then 2's complement 
      @ do not include #81h command)
      @-------------------------------------
      4 1 + 1 + ENTRIES + 255 SWAP - 1 + CHR
      
      @ Apply checksum to START string
      @-------------------------------------
      STARTSTR SWAP + 'STARTSTR' STO
      
      @ Make END string plus checsksum (checksum of end line is always the same)
      @-------------------------------------
      129 CHR 4 CHR + 2 CHR + 1 CHR + 0 CHR + 249 CHR +
      'ENDSTR' STO
      
      @ Make entry PROLOG string
      @-------------------------------------
      @129 CHR 25 CHR + 16 CHR + 0 CHR + 
      @'PROLOGSTR' STO

      @ Send START string
      STARTSTR XMIT DROP 
       
      @ Read and format matrix entries into string
       1 SCNRDATA SIZE LISTç DROP DROP
       FOR chnl      
            @ Get first entry and remove decimal point if present
            SCNRDATA chnl 1 - 5 * 1 + GET çSTR DUP 
            "." POS DUP
            IF 0 >  
            THEN 1 SWAP 1 - SUB "C" SWAP + 'CHANNEL' STO
            ELSE DROP "C" SWAP + 'CHANNEL' STO  END
            @ Get second entry and format to xxx.xxxx, add decimal point
            @ if not present
            SCNRDATA chnl 1 - 5 * 2 + GET DUP 
               DUP çSTR "." POS 
               IF 0 == THEN DROP çSTR ".0000" + 'FREQ' STO
                  FREQ SIZE IF 6 == THEN "0" FREQ + STO END
                  FREQ SIZE IF 7 == THEN "0" FREQ + STO END 
               ELSE
                  IF 100 < 
                  THEN çSTR "0" SWAP + 'FREQ' STO  
                  ELSE  çSTR 'FREQ' STO 
                  END
                  FREQ SIZE 
                  IF 5 < THEN "0" FREQ SWAP + 'FREQ' STO END 
                  FREQ SIZE
                  IF 6 < THEN "0" FREQ SWAP + 'FREQ' STO END 
                  FREQ SIZE
                  IF 7 < THEN "0" FREQ SWAP + 'FREQ' STO END 
                  FREQ SIZE
                  IF 8 < THEN "0" FREQ SWAP + 'FREQ' STO END
                  FREQ SIZE
                  IF 8 > THEN "Invalid Freq: Forcing to 144.3900" MSGBOX "144.3900" 'FREQ' STO END
               END
               FREQ "^F" SWAP + 'FREQ' STO
            @ Third, fourth and fifth entries  
            SCNRDATA chnl 1 - 5 * 3 + GET IF 1 == THEN "^DS" ELSE "^DR" END 'DLY' STO
            SCNRDATA chnl 1 - 5 * 4 + GET IF 1 == THEN "^LS" ELSE "^LR" END 'LO'  STO
            SCNRDATA chnl 1 - 5 * 5 + GET IF 1 == THEN "^PS^" ELSE "^PR^" END 'PRI' STO
            
            @ Concatenate to form full data string
            CHANNEL FREQ + DLY + LO + PRI + 'CURRENTENTRY' STO 
            
            @Calculate checksum for full data string 
            CURRENTENTRY 1 1 SUB NUM 
            2 CURRENTENTRY SIZE
            FOR idx CURRENTENTRY idx idx SUB NUM + NEXT 
            
            @ Make entry PROLOG string (it needs actual message size
            129 CHR CURRENTENTRY SIZE 3 + CHR + 16 CHR + 0 CHR + 
            'PROLOGSTR' STO

            @ Add msg length , command, command argument to
            @ complete checksum
            CURRENTENTRY SIZE + PROLOGSTR SIZE 1 - + 16 + 0 + NEG 256 MOD CHR
            CURRENTENTRY SWAP + 'CURRENTENTRY' STO
            
            @ Add prolog
            PROLOGSTR CURRENTENTRY + 'CURRENTENTRY' STO
            
            @ Send data stream
            CURRENTENTRY XMIT DROP
            
        NEXT 
      
      @ Send END string
      ENDSTR XMIT DROP
      
      @ Clean up directory before quitting (future versions will use
      @ compiled variables)
      'PROLOGSTR' PURGE 
      'ENTRIES' PURGE 
      'STARTSTR' PURGE 
      'CHANNEL' PURGE 
      'FREQ' PURGE 
      'CURRENTENTRY' PURGE 
      'STARTSTR' PURGE 
      'ENDSTR' PURGE 
      'PRI' PURGE 
      'LO' PURGE 
      'DLY' PURGE
   ª
ª